  "documentation": {
    "range": "<em>Gymnothorax javanicus</em>&#160;is widely distributed throughout the Indo-Pacific, from the Red Sea and East Africa (Fricke 1999), east to Mesoamerica (including the Galapagos Islands), north to Hawaii and south to northern Australia. Its depth range is 0-50 m (Sommer <em>et al</em>. 1996).",
    "population": "This species is moderately common throughout its range (D.G. Smith pers. comm. 2011).",
    "habitats": "This species is found in lagoon and seaward reefs and commonly seen along deep drop-offs and slopes in Indonesian waters (Kuiter and Tonozuka 2001).  Juveniles are more secretive and occur on intertidal reef flats (Myers 1999). It feeds primarily on fishes and occasionally on crustaceans.  This is the largest Indo-Pacific moray eel (Kuiter 1998), perhaps reaching 3 m in length.  Because of its position at the top of the reef's food chain it is often ciguatoxic.",
    "threats": "There are no major threats known to affect this species.",
    "measures": "Although there are no species specific conservation measures in place for <em>Gymnothorax javanicus</em>, the vast distribution of this species probably overlaps numerous marine protected areas in the Indo-Pacific.",
    "use_trade": "There are no major fisheries for this species as it is often ciguatoxic. They are occasionally taken for public aquaria displays.",
    "rationale": "<em>Gymnothorax javanicus</em>, a widespread species, is found throughout the Indo-Pacific and the Red Sea from East Africa, Hawaii, Polynesia, the Ryukyu Islands, Cocos Islands, Seychelles, Madagascar, Pitcairn Group, Japan, New Caledonia, Austral Islands, and is also found in the Galapagos Islands. Its depth range is from 0-50 m. This species is moderately common and there are no known major threats. There are no major fisheries for this species as it is often ciguatoxic, although it is occasionally   removed for public aquaria displays. Although there are no species specific conservation measures in place for <em>G</em>.&#160;<em>javanicus</em>,&#160;its wide range also overlaps numerous marine protected areas. It is listed as Least Concern.",
    "trend_justification": null,
    "taxonomic_notes": "<em>Gymnothorax mindonoensis</em> is valid as a synonym of <em>Gymnothorax javanicus</em>."
  },
